From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 13 Sep 2026 16:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] appinfo: request the ACGs Waydroid actually uses

webos_app_generate_security_files turns requiredPermissions into
Waydroid.app.json in client-permissions.d. With the key absent it writes
an empty list:

  { "Waydroid": [] }

so once the app registers it can call nothing that any ACG protects. Both
of the calls it makes are protected:

  user_manager.py   luna://com.webos.applicationManager/launch
                      -> application.launcher
  notification_manager.py
                    luna://com.webos.notification/createToast
                      -> notification.operation

application.operation is what the generator adds for qml apps and what
every other LuneOS app carries; a native app that shows up in the
launcher needs it too.

Pairs with the exeName fix in webos_app_generate_security_files.bbclass -
without that the role never matched this app at all.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS-specific]
---
 data/configs/luneos/appinfo.json         | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/data/configs/luneos/appinfo.json
+++ b/data/configs/luneos/appinfo.json
@@ -5,6 +5,11 @@
     "main": "waydroid.sh",
     "params": "",
     "type": "native",
+    "requiredPermissions": [
+        "application.launcher",
+        "application.operation",
+        "notification.operation"
+    ],
     "uiRevision": 2,
     "vendorurl": "https://waydro.id",
     "icon": "icon.png"
